{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074323-rewrite-history-and-multiple-templates","id":1074323,"title":"Rewrite History and Multiple Templates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-06T14:38:37-07:00","id":1074323,"title":"Rewrite History and Multiple Templates","content":"So. Here's the thing. Rewrite History can remove a template that originated as a Human, like Changeling, Geist or Vampire. And the subject of the spell is then completely functionally human for the duration. Now imagine the subject of the spell, when the spell is active gains another gainable major template. Gets Embraced or something like that. And then Rewrite History is dispelled? What happens to the subject? Does one template overrwrite the other, and if so which one is it? Do the templates just kinda' fuse into something weird? Does the subject become Sam Haight(Ohgodpleaseno)? I wanna know your guys opinions on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T14:58:34-07:00","id":1074334,"title":"","content":"When history returnes to normal so does the subject so the first template would prevail in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Memb